%I A399765 #31 Sep 30 2026 00:11:09
%S A399765 1,0,0,4,0,36,64,468,1792,9262
%N A399765 Number of ways to cut a non-right triangle into n self-similar parts.
%C A399765 For four parts, connect midpoints or use one of three symmedian constructions. For seven parts, combine two of the four for 4 X 4 X 4 = 64.
%C A399765 Special triangles 4-5-6, 45-60-75 and (1,2,4)pi/7 have the same counts up to a(10).
%H A399765 Ed Pegg Jr, <a href="/A399765/a399765.jpg">36 ways to divide a non-right triangle into six parts</a>.
%H A399765 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TriangleDissection.html">Triangle Dissection</a>.
%Y A399765 Cf. A399770 (right), A400462 (30-60-90), A400510 (isosceles), A400511 (45-45-90).
%K A399765 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399765 1,4
%A A399765 _Ed Pegg Jr_, Sep 10 2026
